      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Eligibility watch",
          "heading": "Koli Sewabu says Fiji will follow Mark Nawaqanitawase's possible switch closely",
          "body": "Fiji Rugby's Koli Sewabu said earlier this week that the union is following Mark Nawaqanitawase's possible switch of allegiance closely, after the winger's agent said he was weighing up his options. He is eligible for Fiji and Italy after a three-year stand-down, and the last of his 11 Test caps for the Wallabies came at the 2023 Rugby World Cup. Sewabu says Fiji would have genuine interest. Wallabies coach Les Kiss says he will wait until the end of the year to see where the player sits."
        },
