        {
          "kicker": "Red Roses defeat",
          "heading": "England women's 41-match unbeaten run ends as Canada edge Red Roses 24-21",
          "body": "England women's Red Roses lost their unbeaten streak in Toronto, Canada beating them 24-21 with a late Shoshanah Seumanutafa try three minutes from time. The 41-match run, stretching back almost four years, ended in the WXV Global Series, and Canada are the first side to beat England since November 2022. John Mitchell said: \"I know this group has got more in them.\" Next up is the rematch in Ottawa."
        },
