          "kicker": "Pitch safety",
          "heading": "Louis Rees-Zammit keeps up push to end artificial Premiership pitches",
          "body": "Louis Rees-Zammit is still pressing for an end to artificial pitches in the Premiership, after leg burns he suffered at Saracens. The BBC, the Guardian and SA Rugby Magazine have all carried the demand, and newer coverage repeats it, one headline quoting him: 'Can we please stop' playing on artificial surfaces. No formal decision from Premiership Rugby on the future of artificial surfaces has been reported. For Wales, the issue reaches well beyond one winger, with a growing list of Welsh internationals now playing in the Prem."
